## Phase 2: IR-Matching Bug Fix (synth_keys mismatch)
Status: COMPLETE
Date: 2026-06-08
Description: ~30-50% of HASH_JOIN operators failed JIT compilation because
  FindJoinNodeByBuildTableIndex matched IR JoinNodes whose join conditions
  referenced different tables than the physical HASH_JOIN's build table.
Root cause: FindJoinNodeByBuildTableIndex only checked if the IR JoinNode's
  subtree contained the target table scan, but did NOT verify the join
  conditions referenced that table's columns.
Fix: Added condition validation — after finding a candidate IR JoinNode,
  verify at least one join condition references a column from the build table.
Result (none-split): 558/910 (61%) compiled, up from ~50-75% per query.
Files modified:
  - src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp (FindJoinNodeByBuildTableIndex)

## Table Index Mismatch Fix (split-query support)
Status: COMPLETE
Date: 2026-06-09
Description: Split sub-queries (node-based, relationship-center) re-parse SQL,
  causing DuckDB to assign fresh logical_table_index values (e.g., 0, 1) that
  don't match the IR's original indices (e.g., 7, 2). This caused 84%/72%
  compilation failure for node-based/rc splits.
Fix: Three-part solution:
  1. Name-based index remapping (RemapToIRIndex lambda): maps DuckDB's fresh
     indices to IR's original indices via table name lookup, using existing
     CollectIRTableNameToIndex helper.
  2. Physical-plan-only fallback: when no IR JoinNode matches, derives
     probe_schema, build_schema, keys, and output maps entirely from DuckDB's
     PhysicalHashJoin object. Calls CompileFilterProbeProjectFusion with
     nullptr for filter/join/proj IR nodes.
  3. Swapped-side guard (skip_phys_fallback): blocks physical fallback for
     HJs where IR's probe/build sides differ from physical plan. These would
     produce wrong results because probe_schema and key mapping don't match.
UPDATE 2026-06-10: The physical-plan-only fallback (part 2) was REMOVED.
  Bisection showed it caused 5 of 6 node-based wrong-result failures: it
  compiled probe functions for HJs without checking is_build_side, and for
  HJs whose eids belonged to stale sub-query plans under split execution.
  Single-probe compilation is now IR-path only. If re-attempted later, it
  must (a) skip build-side HJs and (b) be keyed per sub-query iteration.
  The single-probe dispatch path itself remains physical-plan-driven; only
  the IR-less registration path was removed. (Multi-probe chain detection
  is still physical-plan-only — it never needed the IR.)
Signature change: CompileFilterProbeProjectFusion join_node parameter changed
  from const AQPStmt& (reference) to const AQPStmt* (nullable pointer).
Files modified:
  - src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp (RemapToIRIndex, physical fallback, guard)
  - include/jit/ir_to_llvm.h (signature change)
  - src/jit/ir_to_llvm.cpp (null join_node handling)

